    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "You mentioned 'traffic oscillations' and 'jam waves' as part of that instability. In some planning circles, there's talk about how these delays aren't just mechanical or driver-error based, but can feel almost unpredictable or erratic, like there's an external force causing sudden, localized disruptions. From a technical standpoint, is there anything that explains those sudden, seemingly irrational stutters in flow that don't quite fit the standard density models?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
